  "description": "Detection regression corpus (TECH-C6). Each trace in scenarios replays a scenario through PromotionEngine, MicGate.decide, or (engine: \"lifecycle\", T8) PromotionEngine, TeardownHoldPolicy and CallTeardownOracle together on a virtual clock, and fails CI on a deviation from its expectation. legacy_characterization (T17) holds the 20 teams_native_{rewalk,flicker_rewalk,debounce}_end traces scripts/extract_detection_trace.py rebuilt from logged verdicts, and the two synthetic seeds that end on the confirm_provisional_end pseudo-event. They are 4 event structures, 18 of them answer their own end through the pseudo-event, and their opening live event and lone-dwell tick time are constructed, not logged: they pin the provisional transitions and the flicker reverts and are evidence for no end rule. A trace in scenarios may not carry confirm_provisional_end (fenced by DetectionCorpusTests). A reliability claim about end detection cites only scenarios traces that carry a truth label. See README.md.",
